### Setup

We need $f(2020) = \sum_{\gcd(k,2020)=1,\, 1\le k\le 2020} k^3$.

Using Möbius inversion on the coprimality condition:

$$f(n) = \sum_{d\mid n} \mu(d)\, d^3 \sum_{j=1}^{n/d} j^3 = \sum_{d\mid n} \mu(d)\, d^3 \cdot \frac{(n/d)^2(n/d+1)^2}{4} = \frac{n^2}{4}\sum_{d\mid n}\mu(d)\,d\left(\frac{n}{d}+1\right)^2.$$

For $n=2020 = 2^2\cdot 5\cdot 101$, only squarefree divisors contribute. Setting $S = \sum \mu(d)\,d\,(2020/d+1)^2$:

$$f(2020) = 1010^2 \cdot S.$$

### Computing $S$

Squarefree divisors of $2020$: $\{1,2,5,10,101,202,505,1010\}$ (subsets of $\{2,5,101\}$).

| $d$ | $\mu(d)$ | $2020/d+1$ | Term $=\mu(d)\cdot d\cdot(2020/d+1)^2$ |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | $+1$ | 2021 | $+1\cdot 2021^2 = +4{,}084{,}441$ |
| 2 | $-1$ | 1011 | $-2\cdot 1011^2 = -2{,}044{,}242$ |
| 5 | $-1$ | 405 | $-5\cdot 405^2 = -820{,}125$ |
| 10 | $+1$ | 203 | $+10\cdot 203^2 = +412{,}090$ |
| 101 | $-1$ | 21 | $-101\cdot 441 = -44{,}541$ |
| 202 | $+1$ | 11 | $+202\cdot 121 = +24{,}442$ |
| 505 | $+1$ | 5 | $+505\cdot 25 = +12{,}625$ |
| 1010 | $-1$ | 3 | $-1010\cdot 9 = -9{,}090$ |

Cumulative sum:
$$4{,}084{,}441 - 2{,}044{,}242 = 2{,}040{,}199$$
$$2{,}040{,}199 - 820{,}125 = 1{,}220{,}074$$
$$1{,}220{,}074 + 412{,}090 = 1{,}632{,}164$$
$$1{,}632{,}164 - 44{,}541 = 1{,}587{,}623$$
$$1{,}587{,}623 + 24{,}442 = 1{,}612{,}065$$
$$1{,}612{,}065 + 12{,}625 = 1{,}624{,}690$$
$$1{,}624{,}690 - 9{,}090 = 1{,}615{,}600$$

So $S = 1{,}615{,}600$.

### Factorization

$$f(2020) = 1010^2 \cdot 1{,}615{,}600.$$

**Factor $1010$:** $1010 = 2\cdot 5\cdot 101$, so $1010^2 = 2^2\cdot 5^2\cdot 101^2$.

**Factor $1{,}615{,}600$:**
$$1{,}615{,}600 = 16{,}156 \cdot 100 = 16{,}156\cdot 2^2\cdot 5^2.$$
$$16{,}156 = 2^2 \cdot 4039 = 2^2 \cdot 7 \cdot 577.$$
(Here $4039 = 7\cdot 577$, and $577$ is prime — checked against all primes $\le \sqrt{577}\approx 24.02$: not divisible by $2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19,23$.)

Thus:
$$1{,}615{,}600 = 2^4\cdot 5^2\cdot 7\cdot 577.$$

**Combine:**
$$f(2020) = 2^2\cdot 5^2\cdot 101^2 \cdot 2^4\cdot 5^2\cdot 7\cdot 577 = 2^6\cdot 5^4\cdot 7^1\cdot 101^2\cdot 577^1.$$

**Verification:** $2^6\cdot 5^4\cdot 7\cdot 101^2\cdot 577 = 64\cdot 625\cdot 7\cdot 10201\cdot 577 = 1{,}648{,}073{,}560{,}000$, which equals $1020100\times 1615600 = 1{,}648{,}073{,}560{,}000$. ✓

### Final computation

$$\sum_{i=1}^{k} p_i e_i = 2\cdot 6 + 5\cdot 4 + 7\cdot 1 + 101\cdot 2 + 577\cdot 1 = 12 + 20 + 7 + 202 + 577 = \boxed{818}.$$

